  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1981-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(A=y^2+2y-1.\\) The equation becomes \\(\\frac{x}{x-1}=\\frac{A}{A-1}.\\) Cross-multiplication gives \\(xA-x=Ax-A,\\) so \\(x=A=y^2+2y-1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Notice that each denominator is one less than its numerator",
        "Set \\(A=y^2+2y-1\\) and compare \\(\\frac{x}{x-1}\\) with \\(\\frac A{A-1}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
